hexagon: reject a GDN conv chain when a node touches the bytes that the fused op moves
Fold-into: patches/hexagon-fusion/0007-hexagon-htp-gdn-fusions-with-rollback-slots.patch

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus every patch of the series before this one.

The fused GDN_CONV_STEP or GDN_CONV_CHUNK stands at the SILU or at the
first CPY of the chain, at the one that comes first in the graph. Thus the
op can write the output of the SILU at an earlier index than the graph
does, and it reads the projection and the conv weights at a later index
than the CONCAT and the SSM_CONV. The graph allocator can give the bytes of
a tensor with no more readers to a different tensor. A node between the
two positions can then read bytes that the fused op wrote too early, or
write bytes that the fused op reads too late. For example, the allocator
can give the output of the SILU the bytes of s_copy, while the GET_ROWS of
the delta net state reads s_copy between the CPY and the SILU. That
GET_ROWS then reads the conv output as the slot index.

The matcher rejected only one case of this condition: a projection and an
output that share bytes. This patch adds a check of each node between the
two positions of each moved access. Such a node must not read or write the
bytes of the output, and it must not write the bytes of the projection or
of the weights. The check compares byte ranges, and it ignores views,
empty nodes and the members of the chain. It runs when a graph is new to
the graph cache.

